From: Andrey <17542208+osahv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:11:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Mesh: "All" list of every node heard, kept on the SD
 card; glyph-aware names

A node pushed out of the (memory limited) node table is parked in a fixed 64
byte record in /LOGS/mesh_seen.bin, up to 256 nodes. The Nodes tab gets an All
button that lists the nodes in memory first, then the ones from the card, newest
first. Memory nodes are written there on exit so the list survives a restart.
The card is touched with chHeapAlloc'd files and one record on the stack.
Node names in the list are cut by characters and drawn through the glyph table,
so Cyrillic names show as letters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
